Thank you to Maria Gilliland who was the only person to respond to my query.

She has a similar set-up at her firm and provided the following advice.

1) LSM does provide a level of protection when importing disks to ensure di=
sks are not imported to more than one host at a time, however, this can be =
overridden with a -C option.

2) Be very careful when assigning disks to two hosts and importing them as =
volumes are easily corrupted if they are imported onto two machines simulta=
neously.

My conclusion is that it is safest to leave the disks enabled on one machin=
e at a time only.  Instead of using the console to enable the disks, I now =
intend to use "hsxterm" and a script to reassign them to another host and t=
o assist with the "fail over" process.  Before reassigning, I will disable =
