Managers,

Thanks to those that responded. This problem was a little 
strange. I ended up working with HP support.  

I had attempted to connect a VT320 terminal to the serial port, 
setting the "console" variable to "serial" & booting the OS CD, 
but got a message saying "The system does not have a console 
configured" & crash.  Support had me run "ecu" with the dumb 
terminal connected & the "console" variable set to "serial", 
then boot the OS CD.  This worked.  Once I had the Tru64 UNIX 
V5.1B installed I shutdown the system, changed the "console" 
variable back to "graphics", ran "ecu" booted the system.  The 
console worked just fine.  I then shutdown & booted the OS CD.  
This worked as well.  

I don't really know why I had the problem to begin with, since 
I had run "ecu" several times while trying to resolve the 
problem before seeking help.  I'm just happy that it is working 
now.  

