Thanks to Phil Baldwin and Benjamin Ingwersen for their responses.

In summary, a few things to check:

Memory channel adapter card should be revision D02 or higher if DMA is =
enabled. This can be checked by looking for mchan 36 or higher in =
/var/adm/messages - earlier revision adapters cannot perform dual PCI =
address cycles during DMA and can cause failure in the mc.mod device =
driver=20

Ic could be an issue with the IP routing table learning new routes =
through PMTU discovery and ICMP redirects. Disabling ICMP redirectls =
when building the kernel is a workaround for this problem.

In our case, when investigating the above it was seen that the kernel =
config file in /sys/conf did not match the probed values shown in =
/var/adm/messages - the config file had values prior to some changes =
made 6 months or so ago. Booting from genvmunix to re-probe the adapters =
and then build a new kernel with the corrected config file seems to have =
clered the fault.


