Greetings,

The best advice came from the venerable Tom Blinn.  I can't express enough
thanks to this man.   He freely gives his time and thought to our problems.

Unfortunately, most versions of Tru64 version 4.0 have a limitation (0-7) of
how many SCSI ids are used for devices.  

Some suggestions:

Upgrade to Tru64 version 5.x.
Use more controllers.

What I did:

I configured 12 devices as units d1-d6 and d101-d106.  This gave me 12
devices as rrzb8 thru rrzg8 and rrzb9 thru rrg9.   Interestingly, the rrz9
devices were d1-d6 and the rrz8 devices were d101-d106.

I then edited the partition maps to "give" me enough drives.   I know the io
will be concentrated to the same devices but am comfortable with it.

Thanks to all for their suggestions!

Jim


