From: Jim Kurtenbach 
Sent: Wednesday, December 15, 2004 3:10 PM
To: Tru64 Mailing List
Subject: Tru64 version 4.0G on a storage array, scsi id greater than 7

Greetings and Happy holidays!

I again find myself dipping into the communal pool of Tru64 knowledge.

I have an ES40 that I am trying to attach to a SAN.  This system is using
KGPSA fibre controllers, connecting to a brocade switch, connecting to a
hsg80.

I built 10 units, d0 through d10.

Tru64 only sees the first eight, scsi id's 0-7.  I've tried using emxmgr to
remap some id's but he only sees 2 devices, scsi id 0 and 1.

How do I get tru64 version 4.0g to see higher scsi id's?

Thanks in advance.

Jim

P. S. I tried the HSG80's in SCSI-2 and SCSI-3 mode to no avail.   They are
running in transparent failover mode.
