Fellow Tru64 UNIX admins,

We are trying to evaluate Business Copy and see if it will help us =
reduce our cold backup window in our R/3 Environment. We had several =
questions with regards to this tool and wanted to see if there were =
others who had gone down this path and what their experience had been.

a. Are you using Business Copy on EVA5000s with Tru64 UNIX systems to =
reduce your cold backup window?

b. If the answer to the first question is yes, can you share any sort of =
"benchmarks" or timings about how long does it take to clone xxx number =
of Gigabytes of data? Is the process linear or parallel - Does it take =
the same amount of time to clone a 100GB and 1TB or is it linear in that =
it adds up as the number of Gigabytes that one is trying to clone =
increases? Any sort of results/numbers/experiences you can share would =
be great.

c. The Tru64 UNIX OS tends to increment the dsk numbers everytime the =
snapped/cloned VDISKS are presented to the Backup Server. Is there any =
way around it?

d. When we submit the clone command to the SAN Appliance, it comes back =
in a few seconds and lets you know that the job/script has completed but =
the cloning continues in the background. Is there a way, we can tell =
that the cloning operation has completed via scripts/SSSU short of =
signing on to the SAN Appliance and making sure that the yellow bulb on =
each VDISK has gone away or that the operation has completed.

Any and all help will be greatly appreciated.

